<title>COLOMBIA: RESEARCH ALERT-Cementos Caribe recommended.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Cementos Caribe recommended.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombian cement maker Cementos Caribe was highly recommended by brokerage Suvalor because of an expected surge in earnings later this year.</p>
<p>It said a sharp increase in demand for cement in late 1997 could push Caribe's net income up by more than 31 percent over 1996 to a total of nearly 69 billion pesos.</p>
<p>The cement maker, which belongs to the powerful Sindicato Antioqeno conglomerate, is also seen enjoying a 46.6 percent increase in operating income, Suvalor said.</p>
<p>&quot;In the group of (Colombian) cement companies, Cementos Caribe, along with Cementos Paz del Rio, is one of our recommendations for this year,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>((-- Juan Guillermo Londono, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944))</p>
